    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "WHAT THIS DOES NOT SAY. (1) It does not say the OTHER four certificate kinds reconstruct: monomial-bound, Handelman, string-length and int-univariate-poly have no Lean proof yet. (2) It does not say the hypotheses are bound to the query's `(assert ...)` lines. They are minted from the certificate, and that binding is the certificate's own two-stage checker, which re-scans the original assertions. It is the same split the hypothesis-binding audit measures across the LRA routes. (3) It does not say an EXTERNAL checker read the module -- the kernel here is this repository's, so this is the self-checker tier, not the external-artifact tier. (4) Scope is deliberately narrow: the zero-product route handles the DIRECT form only (the disjunctive form needs kernel case analysis) and the product route handles a `Negative` refuted atom only (`Nonpositive` needs `mul_pos`). Both declines have tests. WHY THE CARRIER IS THE POINT. `AxReal` is the legacy axiomatized ordered field and carries this repository's only nonzero trusted-surface row, `axreal: axiom=30`. A refutation checked there rests on all 30. `CReal` is constructed and measures 0 (ADR-0512). Both terms would type-check over either, so the distinction lives entirely in which context the test builds -- which is why the test names the carrier and why the count is pinned.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
      "provenance": {
        "command": "python3 render/producers-py/facts_to_docir.py",
